NOTICE — notebooks/shapefiles/

These geometries are committed deliberately: they are what the demo notebooks read, and a
test geometry that exists only on one laptop is not a test geometry. They do not travel in a
package install — no data ships in the rise-eo wheel (git tracking and wheel contents are set by
different mechanisms).

AT_2018_TRAIN.geojson
  900 Austrian agricultural field parcels, 2018, each carrying a `crop` label. EPSG:31287
  (Austria Lambert); attributes reduced to `fid` + `crop`. Derived from EuroCrops, which
  harmonises national parcel declarations — for Austria, the INVEKOS/AMA data — onto a common
  crop taxonomy. Sampled and reprojected for this repository; not the upstream dataset.

  Licence: CC BY 4.0, not rise-eo's MIT. The code in this repository is MIT; data derived from
  EuroCrops is CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Reuse it with
  attribution and a note that it was modified (sampled, reprojected, attributes reduced).
  Suggested citation: Schneider, M., Chan, A., & Körner, M. (2023). EuroCrops: A Pan-European
  crop dataset. Zenodo. doi:10.5281/zenodo.7851838.

AT_ROI.geojson
s2grid=476da24.geojson
s2grid=4772924.geojson
  Authored for this repository — a demo area of interest over Austria, and two S2 grid cells
  (level 11, ~5 km) each lying entirely inside MGRS tile T33UWP. No third-party data.

  The two cells are NOT interchangeable, and the difference is the whole reason the second
  one exists (spec 58 P2 review, 2026-09-12):

    476da24  — south-east of Vienna (16.034–16.116 °E, 48.106–48.156 °N). Imagery only:
               it lies 47.7 km outside AT_ROI, and the nearest AT_2018_TRAIN field is
               50.2 km away, so ZERO labels fall in it. Use it for single-MGRS-tile imagery
               tests (download, datacube, CRS) that need no labels.
    4772924  — in the Waldviertel (15.390–15.472 °E, 48.482–48.532 °N), inside AT_ROI.
               43 AT_2018_TRAIN fields fall in it across 7 crop classes, and the Austria
               archive covers it with 21 T33UWP granules over 21 dates in Apr–Sep 2018.
               Use it for anything that needs imagery AND labels — e.g. the
               create_training_data leg of runbooks/58-p2-window-a.md.

  Generated with rise_eo.grid.roi_to_s2_grids(AT_ROI, grid_size_km=5).

